From 20b6e75825de6bdff94adebc015afa375058443a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo Sachsenberg <sachsenberg@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 23:04:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [FEATURE] ProSE: keep more peaks per window in dense
 high-resolution spectra (prototype)

Where the local peak filter keeps full quotas (peaks:window_type auto at high resolution, or
jump_full), a spectrum in which peaks:window_top peaks per 100 Da window would remove more than
peaks:dense_intensity_loss (0.2) of its intensity after deisotoping keeps peaks:dense_window_top
(100) peaks per window instead. Low-resolution filtering is unchanged. Both values are recorded in
the search parameters; filterLocalPeaks_ reports whether a spectrum was dense and preprocessSpectra_
logs how many were.

Benchmark prototype for OpenMS#10364; not proposed for merging: the Astral gain on the benchmark
database (+9%) does not hold against doubled search spaces (entrapment and foreign-proteome
controls), see the supplement.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
